{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"}],"modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","title":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder.swift#L101","fileName":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder.swift"}},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On macOS and Linux, make the destination with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which fills in the endpoint, the stream’s API secret, this encoder and the Measurement","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Protocol’s limits:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The encoder is for a server, and is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, as the Measurement","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Protocol takes none of its requests without the stream’s API secret, which must stay on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server: anyone holding it can send events to the property. A server forwarding an app’s events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remakes each ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the app’s identifier, timestamp and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and hands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them to the destination; tracking them again through a tracker with ","type":"text"},{"code":".sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every user as one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request’s body is a JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":" holding one client’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events, oldest first, as the Measurement Protocol takes one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" a request. A batch of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records from several sessions makes a request for each, in the order of each session’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record. The members are:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The records’ session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the first and last 64 bits of the UUID in decimal, joined by a period; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the same way when its context has no session, so each such record is a request of its own","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"consent","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_user_data"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_personalization"},{"type":"text","text":", both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DENIED"},{"type":"text","text":", so Google uses none of the events for advertising"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One object per record: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"params"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s stored properties by name; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp_micros"},{"type":"text","text":", when it was tracked, in whole microseconds since 1970"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"params"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, the first 48 bits of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its version 7 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", so Google Analytics groups the session’s events; it is left out for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session, or a session key of another version."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", no user properties, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_location"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip_override"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_agent"},{"type":"text","text":", so Google Analytics records no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"location or device for the events. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context, and any other context value, aren’t sent. Google Analytics counts a user per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its users are sessions. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"engagement_time_msec"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure engagement, so the events don’t count toward Google Analytics’ engagement time or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"engaged sessions, and its Realtime and Users reports can show no users while events arrive:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"check the event counts instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out. Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans as parameters, so an object or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array is spread into a parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart_size"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags_0"},{"type":"text","text":"), and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", such as an optional without a value or a redacted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element of an array, is left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event or parameter name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"breaks Google Analytics’ naming rules or is one it keeps for itself, one of more than 25","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameters, one with a string over 100 bytes, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one that holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is more than 71 hours before or 15 minutes after the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch is encoded, or has no microseconds form, and one too large for a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","isActive":true},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Google Analytics would answer 2xx to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such an event and, under its default, relaxed validation, store it without the parameter that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"breaks a rule, or under a name it never checked. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"up to 500 characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Google Analytics takes an event up to 72 hours old; the encoder holds records to 71, the hour to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spare for the request to reach Google and for clocks that disagree. Each request’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EncodedRequest\/deadline"},{"text":" is 71 hours after its oldest record was tracked, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops a request still being retried by then, every record of it, the younger ones included, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports it as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"text":", rather than send records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Google Analytics would store as 72 hours old.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics counts each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one it receives: a record sent again, by a retry after Google stored it, by a delivery that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends a cancelled batch again, or by a store’s redelivery after a relaunch, is counted twice. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record a store recovers keeps its session, so it is counted under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"text":" splits each client’s records into requests within the encoder’s limit,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":" by default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for it. The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives, a malformed one or one whose events it doesn’t store included, so a record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder sends is counted as delivered whatever Google Analytics makes of it, and a wrong","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing stored: check the property’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. The bytes are the same for the same records,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the same time, on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their names’ UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/init(plan:limit:now:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties"},{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of Google Analytics 4’s Measurement Protocol, so an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a server can send events to a web or data stream’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/mp\/collect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/requests(for:)":{"title":"requests(for:)","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/requests(for:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"type":"text","text":" as the requests the Measurement Protocol takes, a client’s records in each, within"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder’s limit, with the records left out of them."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"requests","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"for","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchRequests","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13BatchRequestsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0abC5ErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError":{"url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsencodingerror","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"batchLimit","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/batchlimit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol’s limits on one request: 25 events and 100,000 bytes of body, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s included."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding":{"title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"googleAnalytics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"measurementID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"apiSecret","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB6RegionO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"now","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Date","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB10SetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"URLSessionTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations19URLSessionTransportV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/googleanalytics(measurementid:apisecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination on a server that sends batches to the Google Analytics web or data stream of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"measurementID"},{"type":"text","text":", authenticated by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"apiSecret"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSessionTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]}},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"HTTPDestination","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/outcome(of:for:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/outcome(of:for:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"outcome"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations21HTTPTransportResponseV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPTransportResponse"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"for"},{"kind":"text","text